From 05a836d9dd5c0e473284f7a0f325f2320fcf2d93 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 23:22:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 087/112] Filters: unchanged blocks take v17's own loops again;
 ramps per sample in a loop of their own

Finishes the refactor left uncommitted by the interrupted stage, without its
CPU shortcuts. A block whose configuration equals the last one's renders in
the per-layout, per-channel inlined loops of v17 (bit-exact, and as fast as
v17); only a block whose coefficients move takes the shared, not inlined ramp
loop (renderChannelRamp(): one per ladder / SVF variant for every layout and
both channels).

Dropped from the uncommitted draft, as they cost quality the spec rules out:
- steps every 4 samples (a staircase at 11 kHz): the coefficients move on
  every sample again;
- a 1/512 threshold (3.4 cents) below which a change jumped: every change,
  however small, moves (exact comparison, as in 4a95770c).
Kept: the 12 / 24 dB ladders take the cheaper tanh loop (no morph term) while
they move, where morph is 0 at both ends.

filter_neutral (PC): static hash 1b6b22e3ec7a6374 = the source before the
ramps (04c065ea) in all 648 cases; zipper above 2 kHz: SVF -99 -> -112 dBc,
HP ladder -73 -> -83 dBc against the chunked draft.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
